hadiths[9]{hadithnumber,text}:
"19032","Haddathana Waki, haddathana Sufyan from Mukhariq ibn Khalifa al-Ahmasi from Tariq that al-Miqdad said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Badr: O Messenger of Allah, we do not say to you as Banu Israil said to Musa: Go you and your Lord and fight, indeed we sit here. But go you and your Lord and fight, indeed we are with you fighting."
"19033","Haddathana Waki from Sufyan from Alqama from Tariq who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Which jihad is best? He said: A word of truth before an unjust ruler."
"19034","Haddathana Abd al-Rahman from Shuba - and Ibn Jaafar said: Thana Shuba - from Qays ibn Muslim who said: I heard Tariq ibn Shihab say: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I campaigned in the caliphate of Abu Bakr and Umar some forty-odd or some thirty-odd, between raid and expedition - and Ibn Jaafar said: thirty-three or forty-three, from raid to expedition."
"19035","Haddathana Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi from Sufyan from Alqama ibn Marthad from Tariq ibn Shihab that a man asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), having put his foot in the stirrup: Which jihad is best? He said: A word of truth before an unjust ruler."
"19036","Haddathana Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi, haddathana Sufyan from Yazid Abi Khalid from Qays ibn Muslim from Tariq ibn Shihab that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has not placed a disease but He has placed for it a cure, so upon you is cows milk, for it grazes from every tree."
"19037","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Jaafar, haddathana Shuba from Mukhariq from Tariq ibn Shihab who said: Two men became junub, so one of them performed tayammum and prayed, and the other did not pray. They came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he did not blame either of them."
"19038","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Jaafar, haddathana Shuba from Mukhariq from Tariq ibn Shihab who said: The delegation of Bajila came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Clothe the Bajalis, and begin with the Ahmasiyyin. He said: A man from Qays stayed behind, saying: Till I see what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) says to them. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) supplicated for them five times: O Allah, bless them - or: O Allah, bless in them - Mukhariq is the one who doubts."
"19039","Haddathana Abu Ahmad Muhammad ibn Abd Allah, haddathana Sufyan from Mukhariq from Tariq who said: The delegation of Ahmas and the delegation of Qays came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Begin with the Ahmasiyyin before the Qaysiyyin, and he supplicated for Ahmas, saying: O Allah, bless Ahmas, its horses and its men, seven times."
"19040","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Jaafar, haddathana Shuba from Qays ibn Muslim from Tariq ibn Shihab who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I campaigned in the caliphate of Abu Bakr and Umar thirty-three or forty-three, from raid to expedition."
